1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,110
The Prophet (peace be upon him) said:

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:05,730
“Tomorrow I will give the banner to a man at whose hands Allah will grant victory.”

3
00:00:06,310 --> 00:00:07,590
And the surprise was — he was ill.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,780
At the battle of Khaybar, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said:

5
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:12,470
“Where is ‘Ali ibn Abi Talib?”

6
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:13,320
It was said:

7
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,320
“O Messenger of Allah,

8
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:15,510
he is suffering from his eyes.”

9
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,540
So they sent for him and brought him,

10
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:20,880
and the Prophet (peace be upon him) spat lightly in his eyes and made du‘a for him,

11
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:21,680
and he recovered

12
00:00:22,050 --> 00:00:23,240
as if he had never had any pain.

13
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:24,760
(Narrated by al-Bukhari and Muslim)

14
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:28,160
This was one of the miracles of the Prophet (peace be upon him)

15
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:29,660
with which Allah honoured him,

16
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:31,320
and the like of it is not done with patients.

17
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:32,310
But the lesson

18
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:34,730
is that he made du‘a for ‘Ali while he was in pain

19
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:36,010
and did not leave him ill.

20
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:40,020
The Prophet (peace be upon him) taught us that a patient is not to be left alone:

21
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:40,830
du‘a is made for him,

22
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:41,760
he is treated,

23
00:00:41,990 --> 00:00:43,220
and healing is sought for him from Allah.

24
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:46,760
Share this story with someone you love, and follow the channel.

